  "synthesis": "Recent activity centres on machine learning applied to multi-omics and cancer data. Preprints address multi-cohort integration: BARRR, a bidimensional reduced-rank regression tested on simulations and TCGA somatic data, and MINT Block, which jointly integrates multi-omics data across independent studies while modelling study-specific unwanted variation. A pan-cancer benchmark evaluates clustering of patient-specific gene regulatory networks across 9,778 tumors from 33 cancer types. Published items are largely cancer prognostic models, including a five-gene mitochondrial RiskScore in colorectal cancer and a five-metabolite plasma panel in imatinib-treated GIST, alongside an NCI foundation-model workshop report. One review notes limits in generalizability. The rise is recorded as 9 published and 4 preprint items, with a rise ratio of 2.56; no code or industry signals were observed.",
